From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 22:29:45 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Show 360 and VR180 videos as a flat view that the user
 turns

A 360 video is a sphere in one picture, stereo ones two spheres on top
of each other, and VR180 two half spheres side by side. mpv now tells
how the container maps the sphere (track-list demux-projection, from MP4
sv3d and Matroska's Projection); where it does not, the projectionType
that Invidious passes on is used (EQUIRECTANGULAR, MESH).

Turn it with FFmpeg's v360 filter into a flat view of the direction the
user looks in, 100 degrees across one view: both eyes of a stereo video
to the same direction, handed on as full side by side, a mono video as
one picture. Dragging on the video and the arrow keys (with Ctrl they
seek) turn the view through vf-command. The layout is the stream's own
stereo declaration, else the shape of the frame.

